      "source": [
        "# GIL\n",
        "\n",
        "The GIL, or global interpreter lock, is a CPython lock that normally permits only one thread at a time to execute Python bytecode. Free-threaded builds can run without it.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-GIL)"
      ]
    }
  ],
